    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "```\r\ndef f(in1, in2):\r\n    out1, out2, *out3 = in1, in2\r\n```\r\n\r\nGives: `InternalError: Internal compiler error: no starred arg found when splitting starred assignment.` `out3` should end up as an empty list\r\n\r\n---------------------\r\n\r\n```\r\ndef g(in1, in2, in3):\r\n    out1, *out2, out3 = in1, in2, *in3\r\n```\r\n\r\ngives `starred expression is not allowed here`. In principle this shouldn't be a problem, although I can see that optimizing it would be tricky.\r\n\r\n---------------------------\r\n```\r\ndef h(in1, in2):\r\n    out, = *in1, *in2\r\n```\r\ngives `too many values to unpack` at compile time. In Python it's fine provided there's no more than 1 element total when it's run.",
